  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nWhile clouds increase overhead, high pressure is expected to sustain \ndry conditions through the weekend. Despite relative humidity values \nlowering to around 25 to 35 percent each afternoon, light winds will \ntemper fire weather concerns. \n\nA slight chance (around 20% or less) of showers can't be ruled out \nalong and west of the Ohio River as a shortwave passes by on Monday; \nhowever, the continued presence of rather dry air in the low-levels \nshould forestall precipitation development across the bulk of the \nforecast area. Best potential for widespread precipitation chances \narrives mid to late week when high pressure retreats east and a \nsystem directs a front towards the area from the west.\n\nTemperatures are expected to remain above normal through the end of \nnext week.",
